// REJECTS: Unexpected token ''true''
//
// hideProperties / hideStereotype / hideTaggedValue are BOOLEAN-valued: the literal `true`
// or `false`, not the string 'true'. Legend's own diagram serialisations are machine
// written, so the quoted form is what appears when a value is round-tripped through a
// format that has no booleans -- which is most of them.
//
// This is the inverse of neg-domain-property-named-true.pure and belongs beside it: there
// the bare word `true` was rejected because a boolean literal is not an identifier; here
// the quoted 'true' is rejected because a string is not a boolean. Three spellings of one
// word, and each grammar position accepts exactly one of them.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::StringFlag
{
   classView v1
   {
      class: fixture::neg::Person;
      position: (1.0,2.0);
      rectangle: (10.0,20.0);
      hideProperties: 'true';
   }
}
